<title>UK: Clarke raises 1997 UK GDP forecast to 3.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Clarke raises 1997 UK GDP forecast to 3.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK Chancellor Kenneth Clarke said on Tuesday he expected UK 1997 gross domestic product (GDP) to grow by 3.5 percent against a previous forecast of 3.25 percent.</p>
<p>Presenting his budget speech, Clarke left the 1996 GDP forecast at 2.5 percent.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 2774</p>
</text>
